WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.226 --> 00:00:18.850
Winter turned to spring and the weather got much better, though the life of a London cab horse

2
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:19.790
is always hard.

3
00:00:20.951 --> 00:00:23.474
Still I knew I had it better than many.

4
00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.316
I found out just how much better one day.

5
00:00:27.597 --> 00:00:30.640
Jerry's cab and several others were waiting at the edge of a park.

6
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.602
There was a concert in the park that day.

7
00:00:35.904 --> 00:00:39.867
The cabbies knew that lots of people would be looking for a ride home after the music was

8
00:00:39.967 --> 00:00:45.452
over. While we were standing there, a shabby old cab stopped beside ours.

9
00:00:46.573 --> 00:00:49.615
The horse pulling it was an old, worn-out chestnut mare.

10
00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:55.720
She had a dull coat, and you could count every rib on her thin sides.

11
00:00:57.261 --> 00:00:59.984
Jerry had put out some hay for me to eat while we waited.

12
00:01:02.324 --> 00:01:07.348
The wind blew a few strands over toward the other horse, and she stretched out her long, thin

13
00:01:07.448 --> 00:01:08.269
neck to pick it up.

14
00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.933
Then she turned and looked around for more with her hopeless eyes.

15
00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.275
I thought there was something familiar about her.

16
00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:21.600
Before I could figure it out, she looked at me and cried, "Black Beauty!

17
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.400
Is that you?"

18
00:01:23.942 --> 00:01:24.702
It was Ginger!

19
00:01:26.203 --> 00:01:29.026
But it was no wonder I hadn't recognized her at first.

20
00:01:30.107 --> 00:01:31.448
She looked like a different horse.

21
00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:36.670
Her beautiful arched neck was now straight and thin.

22
00:01:37.891 --> 00:01:40.673
Her long, delicate legs were swollen from hard work.

23
00:01:41.894 --> 00:01:47.137
And her face, which had once been so full of life and spirit, now showed only suffering.

24
00:01:48.378 --> 00:01:52.041
She coughed, and I could tell her breathing problems were worse than ever.

25
00:01:52.881 --> 00:01:53.942
What had happened to her?

26
00:01:55.943 --> 00:02:01.207
Our drivers were standing together a short distance away, so I moved a step or two closer so

27
00:02:01.247 --> 00:02:02.268
Ginger and I could talk.

28
00:02:03.468 --> 00:02:06.971
"They rested me at Earlshall for a year or so," she began.

29
00:02:06.991 --> 00:02:10.994
"By then I had recovered enough to be fit for work again.

30
00:02:12.476 --> 00:02:16.619
The earl's son had lost interest in me, so I was sold to a gentleman in the area."

31
00:02:16.639 --> 00:02:19.221
"Was he a kind master?"

32
00:02:19.582 --> 00:02:20.022
I asked.

33
00:02:21.263 --> 00:02:23.164
"He was all right," Ginger replied.

34
00:02:23.185 --> 00:02:26.047
"We got along pretty well at first.

35
00:02:27.388 --> 00:02:31.752
But one day he took me for a longer gallop than usual, and my breathing problems returned."

36
00:02:33.116 --> 00:02:33.556
"Oh no!"

37
00:02:34.037 --> 00:02:34.497
I murmured.

38
00:02:34.517 --> 00:02:40.221
"The gentleman had me rested and treated again, but then he sold me too," Ginger said.

39
00:02:41.522 --> 00:02:43.624
She went on to describe what had happened next.

40
00:02:44.945 --> 00:02:49.788
She'd changed hands several times, always ending up in a worse situation than before.

41
00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:55.332
Each owner had quickly realized she couldn't work hard without her health problems returning.

42
00:02:55.352 --> 00:02:59.916
"Finally I was sold to a man who keeps a number of cabs and horses.

43
00:03:01.292 --> 00:03:04.875
He leases them out to drivers who can't afford their own," Ginger said.

44
00:03:04.895 --> 00:03:10.099
"When he found out about my breathing problems, he decided to send me out with one of his

45
00:03:10.139 --> 00:03:10.979
cheapest cabs.

46
00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.662
The driver doesn't care how hard he uses me.

47
00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:20.446
All he cares about is making enough to pay his lease and have some profit left over.

48
00:03:21.887 --> 00:03:25.290
So I work all the time, never even getting a day's rest."

49
00:03:26.531 --> 00:03:27.251
"How terrible!"

50
00:03:27.612 --> 00:03:27.952
I said.

51
00:03:28.812 --> 00:03:31.914
"But you used to stand up for yourself when you were mistreated, Ginger."

52
00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:36.176
"I know," she said with a heavy sigh.

53
00:03:36.196 --> 00:03:37.617
"But what's the point?

54
00:03:38.978 --> 00:03:42.460
If humans decide to treat us badly, they're going to do it no matter what.

55
00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.742
All we can do is bear it as best we can until the end.

56
00:03:47.943 --> 00:03:50.224
I'm glad you seem to have a kind master, Beauty.

57
00:03:51.485 --> 00:03:54.746
As for me, I look forward to the day when all this will end."

58
00:03:56.467 --> 00:04:00.778
I felt very sad, especially when I remembered what a fine horse she'd once been.

59
00:04:02.079 --> 00:04:04.601
I could think of nothing to say that might make things better.

60
00:04:05.942 --> 00:04:09.145
So I put my nose close to hers, trying to comfort her.

61
00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:13.128
"You're the only friend I ever had," she told me.

62
00:04:15.009 --> 00:04:17.892
Just then her driver hurried over and hopped into the cab.

63
00:04:19.053 --> 00:04:23.216
With a yank at the reins, he drove her away, leaving me feeling very troubled.

64
00:04:26.152 --> 00:04:30.156
It was only a week or so later that a cart carrying a dead horse passed by the

65
00:04:30.196 --> 00:04:30.896
cab stand.

66
00:04:32.558 --> 00:04:35.340
The horse's head hung lifelessly over the back edge.

67
00:04:36.661 --> 00:04:39.324
It was such a dreadful sight that I couldn't look for long.

68
00:04:40.505 --> 00:04:45.549
I saw enough, however, to know that the horse was a chestnut with a long neck and a

69
00:04:45.609 --> 00:04:46.310
white blaze.

70
00:04:48.231 --> 00:04:50.994
I believe it was my friend Ginger lying there in that cart.

71
00:04:52.195 --> 00:04:53.456
I hope it was her anyway.

72
00:04:54.092 --> 00:04:56.439
That would mean her suffering is over at last.
